        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Updates for Chrome 148 beta]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29434</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29434"/>
        <updated>2026-04-09T10:58:55.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://collector.openwebdocs.org/" rel="nofollow">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.17.10) found new features shipping in Chromium 148 beta which was released yesterday. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Canary/behind origin trials/enrollment/isolated contexts, it is not considered here.</p>
<p dir="auto">With this PR, BCD will consider the following 8 features as shipping in Chromium 148:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>api.Credential.isConditionalMediationAvailable_static (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5164322780872704" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.HTMLMediaElement.loading (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.PaymentRequest.getSecurePaymentConfirmationCapabilities_static (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/4727235745546240" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>api.SharedStorage.get (removal) (<a href="https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/45930312b5e9c35bfc5334616153cc7c4a2e10dc" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>css.properties.all.revert-rule (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5146458504429568" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
<li>css.properties.image-rendering.crisp-edges (<a href="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7585405" rel="nofollow">ref</a>) (<a href="https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/dqAs7zmriQQ/m/tmK5bJ9sBQAJ" rel="nofollow">ref2</a>)</li>
<li>css.properties.text-decoration-skip-ink.all (<a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5077600085082112" rel="nofollow">ref</a>)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Updated in a different PR:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>api.PerformanceResourceTiming.contentType</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">This PR misses:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The Prompt API that is also <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296" rel="nofollow">announced as shipping</a>. The spec's IDL is not part of webref / browser-specs, so I filed <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4231402437" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c/browser-specs/issues/2430">w3c/browser-specs#2430</a>. Will see if the spec gets added or if we need manual IDL in the collector for this. I can follow up on this separately.</li>
<li>SharedWorker and Web Serial API for Android. Will also follow up on this separately. Edit: See <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4231611415" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29435" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29435/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29435">#29435</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">See also <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-148-beta" rel="nofollow">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-148-beta</a></p>]]></content>
